ScriptCraft is an independent, clean-room project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or
sponsored by the maker of any other screenwriting application. File format names (FDX,
Fountain) are used only to say which files ScriptCraft opens and saves.

Third-party material

This product bundles third-party material under its own licenses, listed below. The per-file
list (author, source, license) is in ATTRIBUTION.md.

- Ubuntu Light (via the epaint_default_fonts crate) — Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0.
- Hack, Noto Emoji and the egui emoji icon font (via epaint_default_fonts) — MIT, Bitstream Vera,
  OFL-1.1.
- Builds made with craft-fonts (CRAFT_FONTS_DIR) embed Liberation Mono (Regular, Bold, Italic,
  Bold Italic) under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; its licence text ships with release packages
  and is retained in craft-fonts (fonts/liberation-mono/OFL.txt).

Code dependencies

- craft-xml, craft-fonts-build, craft-i18n, craft-pdf and craft-proof come from
  storytold/craft-libs (same owner, MIT OR Apache-2.0).
- Krilla 0.8.2 (https://github.com/LaurenzV/krilla) is used through craft-pdf under
  MIT OR Apache-2.0; craft-libs vendors that version with unwind recovery. Its bundled Compact ICC
  Profiles by Clinton Ingram (https://github.com/saucecontrol/Compact-ICC-Profiles) are CC0-1.0;
  the licence texts are retained in craft-libs.
- PDFs exported without craft-fonts embed Hack (MIT and Bitstream Vera licences), the monospace
  face egui ships; with craft-fonts they embed Liberation Mono (OFL-1.1). Builds made with craft-i18n (CRAFT_I18N_DIR) embed its translation
  catalogs (same owner).
- Three dependencies offer a choice of licences; ScriptCraft uses them under the permissive one:
  r-efi (MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later: MIT), self_cell (Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-only:
  Apache-2.0). `cargo xtask licenses` lists them.
